  "objectives": {
    "content": [
      "Identify words for different types of extreme weather.",
      "Use those words to describe storms, heat and cold.",
      "Describe what happens when temperatures rise or drop."
    ],
    "language": [
      "Produce and use the 15 target words: thunder, lightning, a flood, a drought, an ice storm, a blizzard, speed, a tropical storm, a hurricane, a sandstorm, a tornado, rise, drop, a range, a heat wave.",
      "Use related vocabulary sand and funnel, and content vocabulary predict, cyclone, rotate and supercell to support the target set.",
      "Recognise one-word vs. two-word compound nouns among the storm words (sandstorm, thunderstorm vs. tropical storm, heat wave)."
    ]
  },
